  "description": "The fabric is identified as **default\u2011fabric.region1**, with the display name *Default Fabric Region\u202f1* and assigned to cluster\u202f101. Its management network uses the\u202f10.0.0.0/24 subnet reachable via gateway\u202f10.0.0.1. Loopback addresses are drawn from\u202f192.168.0.0/24, while overlay loopbacks occupy\u202f192.168.10.0/24. The underlay point\u2011to\u2011point fabric links are provisioned from the\u202f172.16.0.0/16 pool, and any PNF service\u2011chain traffic will use the\u202f10.10.0.0/24 subnet. The eBGP ASN pool for the underlay spans\u202f64500\u202fto\u202f64510, and the overlay iBGP ASN is set to\u202f64512. Device authentication relies on the root password **P@ssw0rd!**. The deployment targets twelve devices in an enterprise\u2011style configuration with VLAN\u2011VN uniqueness checks enabled, and configured interfaces will not be imported automatically.\n\nTwo node profiles have been defined: a *leaf\u2011profile* that currently includes the serial numbers\u202fSN1234567890\u202fand\u202fSN0987654321, and a *spine\u2011profile* without any pre\u2011assigned serials. Interface filtering will accept interfaces matching the regular expressions \u201c^ge\u2011\u201d and \u201c^xe\u201d. A supplemental day\u20110 configuration named **base\u2011config** is available, containing the commands `system services ssh; set system host-name {{hostname}}`. The only device slated for zero\u2011touch provisioning is a leaf with serial\u202fSN1122334455, hostname **leaf01.example.com**, underlay ASN\u202f64501, loopback IP\u202f192.168.0.10, management IP\u202f10.0.0.10, and it will apply the **base\u2011config** day\u20110 snippet. The devices run OS version\u202f18.4R1."
}